You're afraid of insects and women.

242
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:24,112
Ladybugs must render you catatonic.

243
00:14:26,156 --> 00:14:28,324
It was a joke.

244
00:14:28,825 --> 00:14:31,202
I made it to lessen your discomfort.

245
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:33,830
You're welcome.

246
00:14:34,748 --> 00:14:36,207
[DOOR OPENS]

247
00:14:39,086 --> 00:14:41,421
Ha-ha. Don't knock. Just walk in.

248
00:14:41,588 --> 00:14:46,088
Why be polite to the world's leading
expert on the dung beetle?

249
00:14:46,968 --> 00:14:49,845
Excuse me,
are you Professor Crawley?

250
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:51,932
Who wants to know??

251
00:14:52,974 --> 00:14:55,393
I'm Dr. Cooper,
from the Physics Department.

252
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:58,062
-Couldn't wait, huh?
-I'm sorry?

253
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:01,775
I haven't even packed yet
and you're already measuring my lab...

254
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:04,903
...for one
of your godless laser machines.

255
00:15:06,405 --> 00:15:09,574
No, you don't understand.
We just wanna ask you a question.

256
00:15:10,575 --> 00:15:12,451
Let me ask you one first.

257
00:15:12,619 --> 00:15:15,705
What's a world-renowned entomologist
with a doctorate. ..

258
00:15:15,872 --> 00:15:18,541
...and 20 years of experience,
to do with his life. ..

259
00:15:18,708 --> 00:15:22,378
...when the university cuts off
the funding for his lab, huh?

260
00:15:23,004 --> 00:15:27,049
Ask rhetorical questions
that make people uncomfortable?

261
00:15:28,009 --> 00:15:29,343
[CHUCKLES]

262
00:15:30,470 --> 00:15:31,762
What's your deal?

263
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:36,430
Are they planning to outsource my job
to Bangalore?

264
00:15:37,894 --> 00:15:39,520
I'm from New Delhi.

265
00:15:39,938 --> 00:15:43,274
-We should find another entomologist.
“We're here. Let's settle this.

266
00:15:43,442 --> 00:15:46,111
Professor,
can you identify our cricket?

267
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:47,320
Of course I can.

268
00:15:47,487 --> 00:15:51,240
I can identify every insect
and arachnid on the planet.

269
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:54,702
Not that that's gonna keep me from
having to move in with my daughter...

270
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:59,370
...In Oxnard. And we're not talking
Oxnard at the beach. No.

271
00:16:00,208 --> 00:16:04,295
We're talking Oxnard
in the onion fields.

272
00:16:07,674 --> 00:16:11,052
-Well, could you look at Toby?
-Toby?

273
00:16:12,637 --> 00:16:15,139
What a stupid name for a cricket.

274
00:16:16,516 --> 00:16:18,142
Told you.

275
00:16:18,810 --> 00:16:19,852
It's a field cricket.

276
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,104
-Yes.
-No, wait.

277
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:23,022
Dr. Crawley, are you sure?

278
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:26,818
Young man, I've been studying insects
since I was 8 years old.

279
00:16:26,985 --> 00:16:29,821
You know what they used to call me
in school?

280
00:16:29,988 --> 00:16:31,781
Creepy Crawley.

281
00:16:32,616 --> 00:16:35,702
Cruel as that may be,
that is not in itself a credential.

282
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:38,997
Let me show you something.

283
00:16:39,873 --> 00:16:42,876
See that?
That's a Crawley's dung beetle.

284
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:45,128
I discovered it after spending
six months. ..

285
00:16:45,295 --> 00:16:47,547
...slogging through
the Bornean rain forests. ..

286
00:16:48,131 --> 00:16:50,091
...while my wife was back home...

287
00:16:50,258 --> 00:16:52,593
...shacking up
with a two-bit ornithologist...

288
00:16:52,761 --> 00:16:57,261
...who lives on a sailboat
and likes to wear boot-cut jeans.

289
00:16:58,475 --> 00:17:02,975
So when I tell you
that that's a common field cricket. ..

290
00:17:03,313 --> 00:17:05,690
...you can take that
to the damn bank.

291
00:17:05,857 --> 00:17:07,483
Because God knows I can't.

292
00:17:07,651 --> 00:17:10,236
That tramp took me for everything.

293
00:17:16,243 --> 00:17:18,703
Well, apparently I was wrong.

294
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:21,873
Congratulations.

295
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:28,546
Enjoy Oxnard.

296
00:17:30,507 --> 00:17:33,426
I'm sure your daughter's looking forward
to having you.

297
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:43,228
Oh, hey, Sheldon.
What you got there? New comic book?

298
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:45,355
Old comic book.

299
00:17:45,522 --> 00:17:48,942
I just retrieved it
from my safe-deposit box.

300
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:51,403
What do you have
a safe-deposit box for?

301
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:54,739
Old comic books.

302
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:59,577
I lost this to Wolowitz
in an ill-considered cricket wager.

303
00:17:59,744 --> 00:18:02,246
What, do they have Wii cricket now?

304
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:05,792
That can't be very popular.

305
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:08,002
Penny, I'd rather not talk about it.

306
00:18:08,169 --> 00:18:12,173
Well, if it makes you feel any better,
I'm not feeling so hot either.

307
00:18:12,632 --> 00:18:14,759
Why would that make me feel better?

308
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,303
I don't know, empathy?

309
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:25,186
I'm just saying that you're feeling upset
about something with Howard...

310
00:18:25,353 --> 00:18:27,271
...and I'm upset about something
with Leonard.

311
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,441
Yes, the disappointing sex.

312
00:18:30,650 --> 00:18:31,984
That's an inexact parallel.

313
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:34,779
You and Leonard can always return
to being friends.

314
00:18:34,946 --> 00:18:38,282
I can never return to a state
in which Wolowitz has not bested me. ..

315
00:18:38,450 --> 00:18:41,119
...like Mrs. Riley's chicken.

316
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:43,288
What's Mrs. Riley's chicken?

317
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:47,458
A chicken that was owned
by Mrs. Riley.

318
00:18:47,626 --> 00:18:51,212
-Okay, forget the chicken.
- I wish I could.

319
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:55,091
No, no.
You may be right about me and Leonard.

320
00:18:55,258 --> 00:18:59,262
Well, of course I'm right. What are the
odds I'd be wrong twice in one week?

321
00:18:59,429 --> 00:19:02,098
No, I mean,
we can always go back to being friends.

322
00:19:02,265 --> 00:19:06,143
I just said that-- This conversation
has started to circle. Meeting adjourned.

323
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:13,192
-Hello.
-Hey.

324
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,236
What's going on?

325
00:19:15,862 --> 00:19:18,865
Oh, you'd like to catch up
on the events of the day. All right.

326
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:22,785
Well, there was a half-hour wait at the
bank to get into my safe-deposit box.

327
00:19:22,952 --> 00:19:25,704
I was forced to talk to Penny
about your sexual problems.

328
00:19:25,872 --> 00:19:29,083
And, oh, yes, in a moment filled
with biblical resonance. ..

329
00:19:29,250 --> 00:19:30,918
...pride wenteth before my fall...

330
00:19:31,086 --> 00:19:35,090
...causing my Flash 123
to goeth to Wolowitz.

331
00:19:35,548 --> 00:19:38,884
Wait a minute.
You talked to Penny about our sex life?

332
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:42,472
Leonard, it astonishes me
how you continually fixate on the trivial.

333
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:45,516
I lost a bet to Wolowitz.

334
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:49,812
-You're saying you talked to Penny?
Yes.

335
00:19:49,979 --> 00:19:52,356
-Interesting.
-Hardly.

336
00:19:52,524 --> 00:19:53,858
Excuse me.

337
00:19:54,025 --> 00:19:55,943
Have I crossed
some sort of line again?

338
00:19:56,111 --> 00:19:57,612
Little bit.

339
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:00,573
Hmm.

340
00:20:04,828 --> 00:20:07,121
Oh. Who cares?

341
00:20:13,211 --> 00:20:15,880
-Oh, hey.
-Hey, what did Sheldon say to you?

342
00:20:16,089 --> 00:20:20,301
Not a lot. That we always have the
option of going back to being friends.

343
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:23,596
-Is that what you want?
- I don't know.

344
00:20:23,763 --> 00:20:25,306
I mean, you have to admit...

345
00:20:25,473 --> 00:20:28,225
...things seemed simpler
when we were just friends.

346
00:20:28,935 --> 00:20:30,102
I guess.

347
00:20:30,603 --> 00:20:33,981
-It would take the pressure off.
- It would, wouldn't it?

348
00:20:35,108 --> 00:20:37,235
So we'll just be friends.

349
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:39,821
Good. Good.

350
00:20:40,697 --> 00:20:42,198
Come here.

351
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:50,457
[BOTH MOANING]

352
00:20:54,961 --> 00:20:57,171
Okay-dokay.

353
00:21:21,404 --> 00:21:23,406
[ENGLISH - US - SDH]

